## Acceptable Differences

Exact JSON pointers and field comparisons are recorded in `review.json`.

- 1021b: author `/exercises/2/tasks/1/domain/3` explicitly includes positive
  post-launch time. FIRST `/tasks/5/equation` with positive upstream time,
  plus `/tasks/5/branches/0`, encodes the same physical requirement.
  Both preserve the meeting 16 km from A and 24 km boat travel from B.
- 1026a: author `/exercises/7/tasks/0/variables` uses circumference in cm;
  FIRST `/tasks/14/unknown` uses m. Models, positive and rejected branches,
  circumference outputs and wheel-turn counts agree under that unit scale.
- 1026b: author `/exercises/7/tasks/1/variables` assigns n to the slower
  shaft; FIRST `/tasks/15/unknown` assigns n to the faster shaft.
  Their domains, periods, roots and shaft-role conclusions agree after the
  stated 400-rpm parameter shift. Raw root strings are not compared as if
  the variables represented the same shaft.
- 1023b: author `/exercises/4/tasks/1/illustrative_model/witnesses/1`
  and FIRST `/tasks/10/extra_assumption_model/witnesses/1` choose different
  second witnesses for the same already-derived nonuniqueness model.
  Equivalent proofs do not require identical witness selection.

## Preserved Caveat

1023b is not repaired or promoted to a unique answer.
Author `/exercises/4/tasks/1/source_caveat`, `literal_model_limit`,
`conclusion` and `conditional_all_remaining_model/restriction` agree with
FIRST `/tasks/10/preserved_source_clause`, `missing_information`,
`requested/disposition` and
`conditional_whole_remainder_not_source_answer/condition`.
Both retain “大部分” and isolate the “全部剩余路程” model as conditional.

